HarnessEntry(id='arc_align_opposite_edge_bar_tracks_from_marker_offsets_and_draw_marker_color_ray', kind='memory', title='ARC: project marker-selected tracks at corresponding offsets between opposite-edge bars', content='For ARC grids with matching segments on opposite parallel edges and sparse markers aligned with one segment, use the examples to identify the bar orientation, segment bounds, colors, and ray extent. A marker selects the track at its offset within the segment; the corresponding track on the opposite segment uses the same offset in the same order, not a reversed offset. Project marker-color tracks only for offsets selected by markers, not for every cell in the opposite segment. Extend a marker-color ray from the aligned edge segment toward each marker and recolor the marker cell to 4 when demonstrated. Preserve both edge bars and unrelated cells. Determine projection direction and extent from the examples rather than assuming all geometry is identical. Validated case: on a 25×19 grid, top segment columns 2–9 and bottom segment columns 11–18 correspond by offset; markers at columns 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9 select opposite tracks at columns 11, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, and 18, while marker-aligned rays extend from the top segment to the markers.', path='arc', scope='global', reference={}, arguments={}, metadata={'scope': 'global'}, source='refine', created_at='2026-09-29T14:58:40.957338+00:00', updated_at='2026-09-29T15:01:51.151Z', version=2)
